title: Rebindable camera keys and button shortcuts
intro: Camera Controls pans with input actions, and a button's Shortcut Action clicks it with one, so every key shows in the Controls window and can be rebound.

project: Empty | Rebindable Keys

chapter: A camera that pans | Camera Controls on the camera
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 1111222211112222\n1111222211112222\n2222111122221111\n2222111122221111\n1111222211112222\n1111222211112222\n2222111122221111\n2222111122221111
deselect
select: Main Camera
add: CameraControls
explain: field:CameraControls.PanWithKeys | Pan With Keys | Camera Controls pans with four input actions: Pan Up, Pan Down, Pan Left and Pan Right. They start on W A S D, the arrow keys and the D-pad.

chapter: Pan keys in the Controls window | Rebind Pan Up to I
menu: Game > Controls...
controls
action: PanUp
explain: controls:usedby | Used by | Pan Up is one of Griff's own actions now, like Jump, and Camera Controls pans up with it.
say: Say the game needs W for something else. The cross takes W off Pan Up, and I goes on instead.
click: controls:remove:W
bind: I
expectcontrol: PanUp = I
click: controls:close

chapter: Play | I pans up, W is free
play
wait: 1
hold: I 1
say: I pans the camera up.
tap: W
wait: 1
say: W does nothing now, so the game can use it. Players can rebind the pan keys too, with a Rebind button.
stop

chapter: A button's key as an action | Shortcut Action
menu: Game > Controls...
controls
click: controls:addaction
actionname: OpenMap
bind: M
expectcontrol: OpenMap = M
say: Here's an action of the game's own, Open Map, on M.
click: controls:close
create: Panel
rename: Map
deselect
create: Button
rename: Map Button
set: Button.Action = OpenPanel
pick: Button.Panel = Map
pick: Button.ShortcutAction = OpenMap
explain: field:Button.ShortcutAction | Shortcut Action | Shortcut Action clicks the button with an input action instead of one fixed key. Its keys are in the Controls window, and players can rebind them.

chapter: Play | M opens the map, then J does
play
wait: 1
tap: M
waitfor: Map | 3
say: M clicks the button, and the map opens.
tap: Escape
waitgone: Map | 3
menu: Game > Controls...
controls
action: OpenMap
click: controls:remove:M
bind: J
click: controls:close
say: Now Open Map is on J, straight away in the running game.
tap: J
waitfor: Map | 3
say: J opens the map. The button follows its action's keys, wherever they're set.
stop
